# Mail app: real email sending via EmailJS (free tier, no backend needed).
# 1. Create a free account at https://www.emailjs.com
# 2. Add an Email Service (e.g. connect your Gmail) -> copy its Service ID
# 3. Create an Email Template with variables: from_name, from_email,
#    subject, message, to_email -> copy its Template ID
# 4. Account -> General -> copy your Public Key
# 5. Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the three values below
# 6. Add the same three as Environment Variables in your Vercel project
#    (Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables), then redeploy
#
# Until these are set, the Mail app falls back to opening the visitor's
# own email client via mailto: — nothing breaks, it just won't send
# straight to your inbox.

NEXT_PUBLIC_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=
